---
import SiteLayout from '../../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';
---
<SiteLayout title="Quest Shogi Privacy Policy" description="Privacy Policy for Quest Shogi, a Meta Quest VR shogi application by Kroma Digital.">
  <section class="page-hero">
    <div class="wrap">
      <span class="eyebrow">App Privacy</span>
      <h1>Privacy Policy for Quest Shogi</h1>
      <p>Privacy information for the Quest Shogi virtual reality application.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="content">
    <div class="wrap prose">
      <p><strong>Effective Date: October 8, 2026</strong></p>
      <p><strong>Developer and Publisher: Kroma Digital</strong></p>
      <h2>1. Introduction</h2>
      <p>Kroma Digital ("we," "us," or "our") respects your privacy.</p>
      <p>This Privacy Policy explains how information is handled when you use Quest Shogi, a virtual reality Japanese chess (shogi) application developed for supported Meta Quest devices.</p>
      <h2>2. Information We Collect</h2>
      <p>Quest Shogi does not require users to create a separate account or provide their name, email address, phone number, or other personal contact information directly to Kroma Digital.</p>
      <p>The application does not include advertising, third-party analytics, or an independent user-tracking system.</p>
      <p>Quest Shogi uses Meta's platform services to verify application ownership and access rights. Meta may process account, device, and entitlement-related information in connection with these services according to its own privacy policies.</p>
      <h2>3. How Information Is Used</h2>
      <p>Meta platform functionality is used to verify that a user is authorized to access Quest Shogi.</p>
      <p>We do not use personal information for targeted advertising, marketing profiling, or selling user data.</p>
      <h2>4. Offline Gameplay</h2>
      <p>Quest Shogi is designed to provide offline gameplay against computer-controlled opponents.</p>
      <p>The application does not require an ongoing internet connection for its core shogi gameplay. However, an internet connection may be required for installation, platform authentication, entitlement verification, updates, or other Meta platform functions.</p>
      <h2>5. Hand Tracking and Device Sensors</h2>
      <p>Quest Shogi supports hand tracking and uses supported Meta Quest device capabilities to enable interaction with the virtual shogi board.</p>
      <p>Hand-tracking information is used to process gameplay interactions. Kroma Digital does not operate a remote service to receive or store raw hand-tracking data.</p>
      <p>Device permissions and sensor access are managed through the Meta Quest operating system and applicable platform services.</p>
      <h2>6. Data Sharing</h2>
      <p>Kroma Digital does not sell users' personal information.</p>
      <p>Quest Shogi does not include advertising networks or third-party analytics services.</p>
      <p>The application integrates Meta platform services for functionality such as entitlement verification. Information processed by Meta is subject to Meta's applicable privacy policies.</p>
      <h2>7. Data Storage and Retention</h2>
      <p>Quest Shogi does not maintain a developer-operated cloud database of player accounts or gameplay histories.</p>
      <p>Any application data stored locally on the device is handled through the application's local storage and the Meta Quest operating system.</p>
      <p>Kroma Digital does not maintain a remote database of personal gameplay records requiring a separate data-deletion request.</p>
      <h2>8. Children's Privacy</h2>
      <p>Quest Shogi is intended for users who meet the applicable age requirements of the Meta Quest platform.</p>
      <p>We do not knowingly collect personal information directly from children through a developer-operated account or online service.</p>
      <p>Parents and guardians should use the parental supervision and privacy controls provided by Meta where appropriate.</p>
      <h2>9. Data Security</h2>
      <p>We seek to minimize the collection and transmission of personal information by providing core gameplay locally on the user's device.</p>
      <p>Platform authentication and related services are handled through Meta's platform infrastructure.</p>
      <h2>10. Third-Party Services</h2>
      <p>Quest Shogi uses Meta Quest platform services.</p>
      <p>For information about Meta's handling of personal information, please refer to:</p>
      <p><a href="https://www.meta.com/legal/privacy-policy/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">https://www.meta.com/legal/privacy-policy/</a></p>
      <h2>11. Changes to This Privacy Policy</h2>
      <p>We may update this Privacy Policy to reflect changes to Quest Shogi, applicable platform requirements, or legal obligations.</p>
      <p>The latest version will be made available through our official website. The effective date will be updated when changes are made.</p>
      <h2>12. Contact Us</h2>
      <p>If you have questions or concerns regarding this Privacy Policy, please contact:</p>
      <p><strong>Kroma Digital</strong></p>
      <p>Website: <a href="https://kroma-digital.pages.dev/">https://kroma-digital.pages.dev/</a></p>
      <p>Contact: Through the <a href="/contact">contact information provided on our official website</a>.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</SiteLayout>
